==English==
{{was wotd|2016|August|6}}
[[File:Nathaniel Ward, The Simple Cobler of Aggawam in America (4th ed, 1647, title page).jpg|thumb|The title page of Nathaniel Ward's book ''The Simple Cobler of Aggawamm in America'' (4th ed., 1647). The word ''nudiustertian'', which Ward coined, appeared in the first edition of the book published in the same year.]]

===Etymology===
L kiko bad not good could not be me wowzers bad

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/n(j)ʊdi.əsˈtɜʃɪən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-nudiustertian.opus|Audio (UK)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|nu|di|us|ter|tian}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|rare|obsolete|modern uses probably|_|humorous}} Of or relating to the [[day before yesterday]]; very [[recent]].
#* {{RQ:Ward Simple Cobler|page=20|passage=[W]hen I heare a nugiperous Gentledame inquire what dresse the Queen is in this week: what the '''nudiustertian''' fashion of the Court; I meane the very newest: with [[eager|egge]] to be in it in all haste, what ever it be; I look at her as the very gizzard of a trifle, the product of a quarter of a cypher, the epitome of nothing, fitter to be kickt, if shee were of a kickable substance, than either honour'd or humour'd.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=“Jet”|title=Jamaica Blue|url=http://www.brewtifulcoffee.com/?p=227|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160410100016/http://www.brewtifulcoffee.com/?p=227|archivedate=10 April 2016|work=Brewtiful Coffee|format=blog|date=14 April 2015|passage=One of the best Chocolate gateau{{sic|gateaux}} I have ever had! And I just had it '''nudiustertian''' afternoon.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=Jaffe Morning Briefing|url=http://www.njtvonline.org/news/uncategorized/jaffe-morning-briefing-aug-21-2015/|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20150906122011/http://www.njtvonline.org/news/uncategorized/jaffe-morning-briefing-aug-21-2015/|archivedate=6 September 2015|work={{w|NJTV}}|date=21 August 2015|passage='''Nudiustertian''' – ''adjective'' Definition: Want a new way to mention something that happened on Wednesday&nbsp;– the day before yesterday? Here you go. Example: “I shared some corned beef hash that '''nudiustertian''' morning.”}}

